<header><p class="st-kicker">sultanate · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Sultanate of the Maldives</h1><p class="st-meta">1153 CE – 1968 CE · capital Male</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An Islamic sultanate of coral atolls in the Indian Ocean that lasted more than eight centuries, famed for its cowrie shells and visited by Ibn Battuta.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>According to Maldivian tradition the king Dhovemi converted from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buddhism">Buddhism</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> in 1153 under the influence of a Muslim visitor, taking the title of sultan. The islands, previously Buddhist, were rapidly Islamised, and Male became the seat of a sultanate that would be ruled by a series of dynasties.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The sultans ruled the scattered atolls through appointed chiefs and the judges of Islamic law. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cowrie-shell">Cowrie shells</a> harvested in the islands served as currency across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a>, and coir rope and dried fish were exported. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-battuta">Ibn Battuta</a> served as a judge in Male in the 1340s and described a court where women sometimes held the throne, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khadija-of-the-maldives">Sultana Khadija</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The Portuguese occupied Male from 1558 to 1573, until expelled by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-thakurufaanu">Muhammad Thakurufaanu</a>. The sultanate became a British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> in 1887, was briefly replaced by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/first-maldivian-republic">First Maldivian Republic</a> in 1953, and gained independence in 1965. A referendum abolished the monarchy in 1968, creating the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-maldives">Republic of Maldives</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/sultanate-of-the-maldives.jpg" alt="Sultanate of the Maldives" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Amit6 · Public domain ·